# The workbook review workspace. Six phases of intermediate workbooks, ~90 one-shot COM
# scripts, working copies and ~30 review renders - 64 MB and 333 files of how the public
# workbook was arrived at, none of which is the product. The reviewed workbook itself ships
# at excel/, and the review's own findings documents are curated into docs/ when they earn
# a place. Keeping the tree locally is useful; committing it is not.
portfolio_model_review/

# Generated build output. The public Excel workbook at excel/ is the REVIEWED artefact and
# is committed; the Python builder writes its own copy here so a build can never overwrite
# it. See docs/excel_operating_model.md.
build/

# Excel and Word lock files. Excel writes ~$Name.xlsx beside a workbook while it is open,
# and a COM session that is killed mid-run leaves one behind.
~$*.xlsx
~$*.xlsm
~$*.docx

*.tmp
*.bak
*.log

# Power BI Desktop writes these into a .pbip when it opens one. They are per-machine
# and per-user, never part of the project definition:
#   .pbi/localSettings.json   machine-bound security-binding signature
#   .pbi/cache.abf            a local cache of the loaded model data
#   .pbi/editorSettings.json  editor state
#   diagramLayout.json        where the tables sit in the model diagram
powerbi/**/.pbi/
powerbi/**/diagramLayout.json
